      {
        "@type": "Place",
        "description": "Elkhorn Slough is a tide-controlled estuary located in Central California, U.S. The estuary\u2019s total length is 11.5 km. Along the length of the estuary, three stations were analyzed: Azevedo Pond (AP), North Marsh (NM), and Vierra Mouth (VM). In particular, AP is located at the head of the slough with the least influence from the ocean, VM is located near the mouth of the estuary with the greatest influence from the ocean, and NM is representative of a midway location across these two stations.",
